NNAAMMEE
     uuaarrkk — Arkmicro Technologies ARK3116 based USB serial adapter

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     To compile this driver into the kernel, place the following lines in your
     kernel configuration file:

           ddeevviiccee uussbb
           ddeevviiccee uuccoomm
           ddeevviiccee uuaarrkk

     Alternatively, to load the driver as a module at boot time, place the
     following line in loader.conf(5):

           uark_load="YES"

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The uuaarrkk driver supports Arkmicro Technologies ARK3116 based serial
     adapters.

HHAARRDDWWAARREE
     The uuaarrkk driver supports the following adapters:

     ••   HL USB-RS232
     ••   HugePine USB-UART
     ••   KQ-U8A Data Cable
     ••   Skymaster USB to RS232

FFIILLEESS
     /dev/ttyU*       for callin ports
     /dev/ttyU*.init
     /dev/ttyU*.lock  corresponding callin initial-state and lock-state de‐
                      vices

     /dev/cuaU*       for callout ports
     /dev/cuaU*.init
     /dev/cuaU*.lock  corresponding callout initial-state and lock-state de‐
                      vices

SSEEEE AALLSSOO
     tty(4), ucom(4), usb(4)

HHIISSTTOORRYY
     The uuaarrkk device driver first appeared in OpenBSD 4.0.  The first FreeBSD
     release to include it was FreeBSD 7.0.

AAUUTTHHOORRSS
     The uuaarrkk driver was written by Jonathan Gray <_j_s_g_@_o_p_e_n_b_s_d_._o_r_g>.

CCAAVVEEAATTSS
     Setting hardware flow control is not currently supported.  It is not yet
     known how to ask the hardware to send a break.

     Arkmicro Technologies do not reply to requests of documentation for their
     products.

